# manual-qa/.env.example — safe template for the manual QA flow.
#
# This file is committed to the repository as the documentation of every
# environment variable the manual QA scripts read from a local dotenv
# file. It contains NO real secrets; every value is a placeholder.
#
# Copy this file to `manual-qa/.env` to provide values to the scripts:
#
#   cp manual-qa/.env.example manual-qa/.env
#   chmod 0600 manual-qa/.env
#   # then edit manual-qa/.env to fill in your real API key
#
# `manual-qa/.env` is matched by the root `.gitignore` and will never
# be committed. The scripts refuse to read it unless it is owned by the
# current user and is mode 0600.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exactly ONE LLM mode must be active. Pick one group and leave the other
# blank. The scripts fail closed when both groups are set or when neither is.
#
# Mode A — inline LLM (model + API key + usage id all supplied locally):
#   OPENHANDS_LLM_MODEL       e.g. openai/gpt-4o-mini (literal default below)
#   OPENHANDS_LLM_API_KEY     your key (required when Mode A is active)
#   OPENHANDS_LLM_USAGE_ID    a label the LLM provider sees for billing
#   OPENHANDS_LLM_BASE_URL    OPTIONAL — override only when your provider
#                             is not the default OpenAI-compatible endpoint;
#                             leave blank to use the built-in default.
#
# Mode B — server-side agent profile id (the Executor pulls the profile
# from the State Registry; no inline key reaches the Executor):
#   OPENHANDS_AGENT_PROFILE_ID
#
# The two modes are mutually exclusive. Setting both is a hard error.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Mode A: inline LLM ---------------------------------------------------
OPENHANDS_LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
OPENHANDS_LLM_API_KEY=
OPENHANDS_LLM_USAGE_ID=flowai-manual-qa
OPENHANDS_LLM_BASE_URL=

# --- Mode B: server-side agent profile ------------------------------------
OPENHANDS_AGENT_PROFILE_ID=

# --- Optional prompt override for ./03-submit-task.sh ---------------------
# When set, ./03-submit-task.sh uses this value in place of argv[1].
# Leave blank to require the prompt on the command line.
PROMPT=

# --- Runtime locations ----------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state root. Mode 0700; every state file is written mode 0600 by
# the scripts. Override only when you want artifacts somewhere else.
FLOWAI_MANUAL_QA_RUN_DIR=/tmp/flowai-manual-qa

# Repository root used by ./01-prepare.sh to `go build` the binaries.
# Leave blank to auto-detect as `<manual-qa>/..`.
FLOWAI_REPO_ROOT=

# Rootless Podman socket. Leave blank to use the standard
# `/run/user/<uid>/podman/podman.sock`. Override only for non-default
# runtimes; the manual QA flow does NOT support Docker.
DOCKER_SOCKET_PATH=

# OpenHands host port range (TCP, 127.0.0.1). The Executor assigns ports
# inside this range when it materialises an OpenHands V1 container.
OPENHANDS_HOST_PORT_START=18000
OPENHANDS_HOST_PORT_END=18010

# In-container workspace path. The Executor does NOT bind-mount the host
# checkout; this value is forwarded verbatim to the OpenHands V1 child.
OPENHANDS_WORKSPACE=/workspace/project

# --- run-all.sh behaviour -------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to skip the EXIT-trap cleanup in ./run-all.sh. Leave blank
# (or set to 0) to run the cleanup at the end of every `./run-all.sh`.
RUN_ALL_NO_CLEANUP=